# Touristo — Architecture Map

This document is the single source of truth for how screens, tech layers, and data connect. Refer to this before creating new screens, routes, or database changes.

## 1. Screen Flow & Navigation

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Splash["Splash Screen (1-2 sec, logo + tagline)"] -->|first-time user| Onboarding
    Splash -->|returning user| Home

    Onboarding["Onboarding Carousel (skippable, cinematic slides)"] --> Home

    Home["Home / Discover"] --> Search["Search Results"]
    Home --> Explore["Destination Explore Page"]
    Home --> HostList["Host Discovery Tab"]
    Home --> Notifications

    Search --> PackageDetail["Package Detail"]
    Explore --> PackageDetail
    Explore -->|Ask AI about destination| TripPlanner["AI Trip Planner (shared chatbot)"]

    PackageDetail --> Booking["Booking & Payment"]
    PackageDetail --> HostProfile["Host Profile"]
    Booking --> MyTrip["Booking Confirmation / My Trip"]

    MyTrip --> Weather["Live Weather & Road Status"]
    MyTrip --> SOS["Emergency SOS"]
    MyTrip --> LiveLocation["Live Location (self-position map)"]
    MyTrip --> Review["Post-Trip Review"]

    HostList --> HostProfile
    HostProfile --> PackageDetail

    Home --> TripPlanner
    TripPlanner --> PackageDetail

    Login["Sign-Up / Login"] --> Home
    Home --> Profile["Traveler Profile & Settings"]

    CompanyReg["Company Registration"] --> CompanyDash["Company Dashboard"]
    Login --> CompanyReg

    %% New Host-Side Flows
    CompanyDash --> HDashboard["Host Dashboard (/host-dashboard)"]
    CompanyDash --> HPackages["My Packages (/my-packages)"]
    CompanyDash --> HBookings["Host Bookings (/bookings)"]
    HBookings --> MyTrip
```

## 2. Technical Architecture (System Layers)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Client["Frontend — React + Vite + Tailwind"]
        UI["Screens (Splash, Onboarding, Home, Search, etc.)"]
    end

    subgraph Server["Backend — Node.js + Express"]
        API["REST API Routes"]
        Controllers["Controllers"]
        Models["Models"]
        AILayer["AI Layer (Trip Planner, Ranking, Summarizer, Comparison, Recommendations)"]
    end

    subgraph Cloud["Supabase"]
        RDS[("Database — PostgreSQL")]
        OSS["Storage — Images, Video Storage"]
        ECS["Functions — Hosting"]
        CDN["Realtime — Real-time updates"]
        WAF["Auth — Authentication & Authorization"]
    end

    UI -->|HTTP requests| API
    API --> Controllers
    Controllers --> Models
    Controllers --> AILayer
    Models -->|SQL queries| RDS
    UI -->|images/video| CDN
    CDN --> OSS
    Server --> ECS
    WAF --> ECS
```

## 3. Database Entities (Core Tables)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ BOOKINGS : makes
    USERS ||--o{ REVIEWS : writes
    HOSTS ||--o{ PACKAGES : offers
    HOSTS ||--o{ REVIEWS : receives
    PACKAGES ||--o{ BOOKINGS : booked_in
    PACKAGES }o--|| DESTINATIONS : located_in

    USERS {
        int id
        string name
        string email
        string password_hash
        string phone
    }
    HOSTS {
        int id
        string company_name
        boolean verified
        float rating_score
    }
    PACKAGES {
        int id
        int host_id
        int destination_id
        string title
        decimal price
        text itinerary
    }
    BOOKINGS {
        int id
        int user_id
        int package_id
        date travel_date
        string status
    }
    REVIEWS {
        int id
        int user_id
        int host_id
        int rating
        text comment
    }
    DESTINATIONS {
        int id
        string name
        string category
        text history
        text culture
    }
```

